structured_output.generality:
This helps any hash join whose bloom filter is pushed into a probe-side scan and whose build keys are dense integers. That is typical of surrogate keys and foreign-key joins against a filtered dimension or parent table, in star and snowflake schemas and multi-key joins (the filter is on the first key). It applies to INTEGER, BIGINT, SMALLINT, TINYINT, UTINYINT, USMALLINT, UINTEGER and DATE keys.

It does not apply to:
- strings, floats, HUGEINT, UBIGINT and other non-integer keys, which keep the hashed filter;
- sparse key ranges (more than 128 bits per build row, or a range of 2^31 or more);
- external (spilling) hash joins and perfect hash joins, which never build a BF;
- joins where the probe column needs a cast.
